  "content": {
    "id": "p51-q4-group-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "True or False? Let $A$ and $B$ be sets in a universal set $U$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p51-q4-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$A\\cup B=U$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. Elements of $U$ may lie outside both sets. For example, let $U=\\{1,2\\}$ and $A=B=\\{1\\}$. Then $A\\cup B=\\{1\\}\\ne U$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q5-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$A\\cup B=B\\cup A$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. Both sides contain exactly the elements in $A$ or $B$, including elements in both.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q6-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$A\\cap B=B\\cap A$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. Both sides contain exactly the elements common to $A$ and $B$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q7-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$A\\cap\\overline B=B\\cap\\overline A$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. The left side contains elements in $A$ only; the right contains elements in $B$ only. For $U=\\{1\\}$, $A=\\{1\\}$ and $B=\\varnothing$,\n$$\\begin{align*}A\\cap\\overline B&=\\{1\\},\\\\B\\cap\\overline A&=\\varnothing.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q8-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$A\\cap\\overline B=(A\\cup B)\\cap\\overline B$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. Intersecting $A\\cup B$ with $\\overline B$ removes every element in $B$, leaving exactly the elements of $A$ outside $B$. These form $A\\cap\\overline B$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q9-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$A\\cap\\overline B=A\\cap\\overline{(A\\cap B)}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. Among elements of $A$, the elements belonging to $A\\cap B$ are exactly those in $B$. Excluding them leaves the elements of $A$ outside $B$ on both sides.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q10-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$A\\cup\\overline A=U$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. Every element of $U$ is either in $A$ or outside $A$, so the union contains all of $U$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q11-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$A\\cap\\overline A=\\varnothing$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. No element can be both in $A$ and outside $A$, so the intersection is empty.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q12-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\overline{A\\cup B}=\\overline A\\cup\\overline B$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. Let $U=\\{1,2\\}$, $A=\\{1\\}$ and $B=\\{2\\}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\overline{A\\cup B}&=\\overline{\\{1,2\\}},\\\\\\overline{A\\cup B}&=\\varnothing,\\\\\\overline A\\cup\\overline B&=\\{2\\}\\cup\\{1\\},\\\\\\overline A\\cup\\overline B&=\\{1,2\\}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe two sets differ.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q13-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\overline{A\\cap B}=\\overline A\\cap\\overline B$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. Let $U=\\{1,2\\}$, $A=\\{1\\}$ and $B=\\{2\\}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\overline{A\\cap B}&=\\overline{\\varnothing},\\\\\\overline{A\\cap B}&=\\{1,2\\},\\\\\\overline A\\cap\\overline B&=\\{2\\}\\cap\\{1\\},\\\\\\overline A\\cap\\overline B&=\\varnothing.\\end{align*}$$\nThe two sets differ.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q14-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$\\overline{A\\cup B}=\\overline A\\cap\\overline B$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. Being outside $A\\cup B$ means being outside both $A$ and $B$. These are exactly the elements common to $\\overline A$ and $\\overline B$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q15-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$A\\cap(A\\cup B)=A$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. The union $A\\cup B$ contains every element of $A$. Intersecting it with $A$ therefore leaves exactly $A$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q16-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "$(A\\cap B)\\cup(A\\cap\\overline B)=A$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. $A\\cap B$ contains the elements of $A$ inside $B$, and $A\\cap\\overline B$ contains those outside $B$. Together these two parts contain all and only the elements of $A$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q17-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "$(A\\cap B)\\cup(\\overline A\\cap B)=A$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. The left side equals $B$.",
          "worked": "False. The two intersections contain the elements of $B$ inside $A$ and outside $A$. Their union is therefore $B$, which need not equal $A$. For example, $A=\\{1\\}$ and $B=\\{2\\}$ in $U=\\{1,2\\}$ give a left side of $\\{2\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      }
    ]
  },
